course: dictionary
lesson: 11827
title: Informal words and slang
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are chatty and informal. You will meet them in magazines, adverts and casual talk, but not usually in school writing. «Biz» is one of these words. It is a short, clipped form of «business».
explain: Context helps you work out the meaning. «She wants to work in show biz when she grows up.» Show biz is about films, TV and theatre, so biz must mean the entertainment industry here.
explain: Slang can also mean something different. «That goal was the biz!» Nobody is talking about an industry here. In UK slang, «the biz» means the very best, so the writer is praising the goal.
fact: Biz is an informal, short form of business.
fact: «Show biz» or «showbiz» means the world of films, TV and theatre.
fact: «The biz» can mean the entertainment or music industry.
fact: In UK slang, «that's the biz» means that something is the very best.
fact: Informal words like biz show the style is casual, so you should not use them in school writing.
exercise: «She wants to work in show biz when she grows up.» What does biz mean here? | * The entertainment industry | A bus stop | A type of office | A short, quiet holiday
exercise: «Show biz» is short for which longer word? | showroom | show bus | * show business | show bizarre
exercise: «That goal was the biz!» What does the biz mean here? | The place where goals are kept | The worst thing ever | * The very best | A loud noise
test: «My cousin has been in the biz for ten years, working on TV shows.» What does the biz mean? | * The entertainment industry | The very best | The school canteen | The bus station
test: Which word is slang and would not be used in a school essay? | * biz | entertainment | business | industry
exam: Why would a writer use «biz» in a magazine article instead of in a school essay? | Because it means exactly the same as every other word | Because it is only used in maths lessons | Because it is the correct word for every formal report | * Because it is informal and chatty, and the style is casual
